+	 * on a Fairphone 3, the same control read (0,0)/1920x1080 after a
+	 * 1080p capture and (0,0)/4032x3024 after a full-resolution one. The
+	 * active area is a property of the hardware and reads the same either
+	 * way.
+	 *
+	 * AfWindows is documented as being in ScalerCropMaximum pixels, which
+	 * on a pipeline that can crop is the active area seen through whatever
+	 * the scaler can reach. The simple pipeline handler publishes no such
+	 * property, so there is nothing there for an application to read;
+	 * naming the space in the control's own maximum is what makes it
+	 * usable, and on this pipeline the two spaces coincide.
+	 *
+	 * The mapping in selectZones() assumes the stream covers the active
+	 * area. A sensor mode that crops rather than scales would need
+	 * analogCrop, which is only known for the format the IPA was
+	 * initialised with and so cannot be relied on here.
+	 *
+	 * The minimum is one pixel rather than the empty rectangle, because a
+	 * window with no area selects no zone and is not something an
+	 * application can usefully ask for. The maximum, which is also the
+	 * default, is the whole area - metering everything, as if no window
+	 * had been given.
+	 *
+	 * Without a size there is no coordinate space to name, so the control
+	 * is not offered at all rather than offered with bounds that mean
+	 * nothing.
